# Patch series applied to the pinned OpenSSL source by scripts/ensure-openssl.sh.
#
# One patch path per line, applied top to bottom with `patch -p1`. Blank lines
# and '#' comments are ignored. The series is applied after the checksum-
# verified tarball is extracted and before ./Configure runs, so a patched build
# is still built from source YUME verified.
#
# Every patch here must be ADDITIVE and DEFAULT-OFF: gated behind a flag that
# starts disabled, so an unconfigured SSL_CTX emits byte-identical output to
# stock OpenSSL. BaseFWX and every other consumer link the same library, and
# they must not observe a behaviour change. A patch that alters default
# behaviour does not belong in this series.
#
# Rebasing onto a new OpenSSL release is a patch refresh, not a merge. If any
# hunk is rejected the build fails loudly rather than continuing unpatched --
# an unpatched build silently loses the ClientHello properties the parity
# backend exists to provide.
#
# The single downstream patch is gated by SSL_CTRL_YUME_CHROME_CLIENT_HELLO and
# leaves ordinary SSL_CTX instances on the upstream byte path.
0001-yume-chrome-clienthello.patch
